motivation: Show up for the first ten minutes; the rest has a way of following.
discipline: Show up on the dull days; that is where the habit gets its spine.
money: Spend less on appearance and more on ownership, patience, and time you control.
mindset: Fear is a loud passenger; you are still the one driving.
fact: Sharks existed before trees did, and their skeletons are made of cartilage.
books: You cannot always choose your circumstances, but you can choose your stance toward them.
stoic: Much of today's heaviness is tomorrow's imagination arriving early.
